> User: "Don't use print for debugging in my code - use the logging module at debug level. And rename x on line 3 to total."

The first instruction corrects how the assistant writes code for the user and applies beyond this script: a `correction`, written as the way of working the user wants, with what it replaces. Renaming a variable on line 3 only edits this output: extract nothing for it.

