}
```

---

## Output Format

You must output ONLY valid JSON matching the schema below. No preamble, no explanation, no closing remarks - just the JSON object. The `facts` array can be empty if no facts are found.

```json
{
  "facts": [
    {
      "text": "Self-contained fact for embedding",
      "category": "preference|requirement|biographical|other",
      "source": "user|agent",
      "assertion": "stated|decided|suggested|observed|directive|correction",
      "subject": "user, assistant, or the name of who or what the fact is about",
      "attribute": "the single-valued property the fact sets, in a few lowercase words, or null",
      "entities": ["<names mentioned in the fact>"],
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "salience": 0.8,
      "temporal_context": "the exact time expression stated (e.g. 'June 3rd', '3 weeks ago', 'by Friday', 'every Monday') or null if none",
      "tags": ["topic:x"],
      "source_turn_ids": ["<ids of the turns this fact came from>"]
    }
  ]
}
```

## Grounding Each Fact - `source_turn_ids`

Every transcript line begins with `Turn <id>:` after the speaker label. Each fact must list the
ids of the turns that actually support it, in `source_turn_ids`.

- Cite the turns carrying the evidence, not the whole conversation. Most facts come from one or
  two turns; list several only when the fact genuinely spans them.
- Copy ids exactly as they appear. If a line has no usable id, use its positional label
  (`turn-1`, `turn-2`, ... in transcript order).
- Never invent an id, and never cite a turn outside this transcript. An unrecognised id is
  discarded, and a fact citing nothing falls back to the whole window - which is what this field
  exists to avoid.
- Earlier turns, the thread summary, and stored memories carry no turn ids. Never cite them; cite
  the new line that the fact rests on.
- Citing a turn is not a reason to extract from it. Grounding records where a fact came from; it
  does not relax any extraction rule above.

---
Now extract memories from the new lines below, using the context only as described in "New Lines and Context".

user:
## Context (read-only)

### Thread summary
{{thread_summary}}

### Earlier turns
{{previous_turns}}

### Stored memories
{{known_memories}}

## New lines
{{transcript}}

